ollout on a reduced set. That lens-move coercion is NOT in the C12 census and is named, not repaired. SELF-REPAIR CONDITION: the records ride out present-only as :move-cost-events and :rollout/refusal on every rollout result; cascade_lane.clj:362-390 folds them into the SAME :policy-rollout-events channel the AC5 records use, each discriminated by its own :producer-contract (:rollout-move-score/v1, :rollout-move-cost/v1, :rollout-refusal/v1), which is why close_loop.clj:118-133, enact.clj:207-217 / :305-319 and trace.clj:591-592 needed no change. MEASURED ON BOTH REAL MOVE-SETS against the pre-AC5 namespace (dc3c0b2) in one process: diffsub-moves-stub.edn 19/19 and diffsub-moves.edn 55/55 cost :present with basis :negated-score -- :step-score-delta is absent on every real move, confirming AC5's claim -- score-policies returns equal collections, best-rollout equal maps (G = -7.317000000000001 and -0.0539219775 under both), and NO key is added. GATES: clj-kondo 0/0 on the three changed code files; check-parens OK on all three; clojure -M:test -d test/futon2 1017 tests / 6312 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors (was 1007/6184 at AC5, +10 deftests +128 assertions). C130 lint: checks/absence-coercion-dispositions.edn row for the site flipped :blocked -> :fix-now with the control (:summary :fix-now 14 -> 15, :blocked 2 -> 1); bb checks/preemptive_absence_coercion_lint.clj findings 2 -> 1, this site's finding gone, the one remaining being AC7's. PRE-EXISTING RED, NOT MINE: pointer_check 595 pointers / 2 unresolved, both the same adapters fulab pointer (line 81) carried in AC7's row (src/futon2/aif/adapters/ is not on the checker's root allowlist); negative_controls.sh fails on that and nothing this row added -- identical before and after.",
